# Phase 2: Cloud MVP

## Overview

Build cloud backend: Go ingest API (direct to ClickHouse Cloud, NO NATS), React/Next.js dashboard with cost attribution, WorkOS auth, and Rust sync daemon. First revenue at Week 8. Deploy on Railway/Fly.io (no K8s). Manual billing for first 10 customers (no Stripe yet).

**Red team changes applied:**
- NO NATS JetStream — direct Go→ClickHouse Cloud batch insert. NATS added in Phase 3 when waste detector consumer exists
- NO self-managed ClickHouse cluster — ClickHouse Cloud single instance. Scale to cluster when >1M events/day
- NO Kubernetes — deploy Go service on Railway or Fly.io. K8s when >10 services
- NO Stripe — manual invoicing for first 10 Pro customers. Stripe in Phase 3
- Tenant isolation: Go middleware enforces tenant_id from JWT (not ClickHouse row policies — row policies broken for shared-service arch)
- Server MUST override client-supplied tenant_id from auth context — never trust client protobuf tenant_id
- Auth: short-lived tokens (24h) via WorkOS, not long-lived device certs. Revocation = token expiry. mTLS deferred to Phase 5 enterprise
- Dashboard: 3 pages (overview + projects + settings), not 8. Add remaining pages in Phase 3
- Landing page + docs site: GitHub README is the landing page

## Context

- [Architecture Review](./architecture-review.md) — Ingest Tier, ClickHouse Schema, Dashboard sections
- Phase 1 provides: protobuf event schema, mmap ring buffer, CLI binary

## Requirements

**Functional:**
- Sync daemon in CLI: drain mmap ring buffer → cloud API (adaptive batching)
- Go ingest API: receive events, validate schema, rate-limit, publish to NATS
- NATS JetStream: durable event streams per tenant, 7-day retention
- Analytics writer: NATS consumer → ClickHouse batch insert
- ClickHouse: events table + 5 materialized views for dashboard queries
- Row-level tenant isolation via ClickHouse row policies
- React dashboard: 8 pages (overview, projects, developers, productivity, waste, security, policies, settings)
- WorkOS auth: OIDC login, organization → tenant_id mapping, RBAC (admin/manager/dev/viewer)
- `codeflow login` — authenticate + provision device certificate
- `codeflow sync` — manual sync trigger
- `codeflow status` — show sync health

**Non-functional:**
- Ingest API: <10ms p99, 50K events/sec/pod
- ClickHouse dashboard queries: <500ms p99 (via materialized views)
- Dashboard TTFB: <50ms globally (edge CDN)
- Dashboard LCP: <1.5s
- Event pipeline latency: <60s end-to-end (event → dashboard visible)
- 99.9% uptime SLA for ingest API
- Offline resilience: CLI works fully offline, syncs on reconnect

## Architecture

```
CLI (Rust)                    Cloud
┌──────────┐                 ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ mmap ring│  HTTP/2+proto   │ Envoy/Caddy → Rate Limiter → Validator│
│ buffer   │──────────────→  │      │                                 │
│          │  mTLS           │ NATS JetStream                        │
│ Sync     │  adaptive batch │      ├→ Analytics Writer → ClickHouse │
│ Daemon   │  (50ev/30s/512K)│      ├→ (Phase 5: Security Scanner)  │
└──────────┘                 │      └→ (Phase 3: Waste Detector)     │
                             │                                        │
                             │ Query API (Go) ← Dashboard (Next.js)  │
                             │ WorkOS Auth ← SSO/OIDC                │
                             └────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

