## Implementation Steps

### Week 1-2: Sync Daemon + Ingest API

1. Implement sync daemon in `cli/crates/cli/src/sync.rs`:
   - Read events from mmap ring buffer
   - Adaptive batching: flush on 50 events OR 30s OR 512KB
   - Protobuf encode → gzip compress → HTTP/2 POST
   - mTLS with device certificate (provisioned on `codeflow login`)
   - Exponential retry: 1s → 2s → 4s → 8s → max 5min
   - Circuit breaker: 5 consecutive failures → store-only mode, retry after 10min
   - Offline buffer: max 100MB, FIFO drain on reconnect, LRU evict oldest if full
2. Implement `codeflow login` in `cli/crates/cli/src/auth.rs`:
   - Open browser for WorkOS OIDC flow
   - Store auth token + device cert at `~/.config/codeflow/`
   - Refresh token automatically
3. Set up Go module (`cloud/go.mod`) with dependencies:
   - `github.com/nats-io/nats.go` — NATS client
   - `github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-go/v2` — ClickHouse driver
   - `google.golang.org/protobuf` — protobuf runtime
   - `github.com/prometheus/client_golang` — metrics
4. Implement ingest API (`cloud/cmd/ingest/main.go`):
   - `POST /v1/events` — receive EventBatch protobuf
   - mTLS device cert validation middleware
   - Token-bucket rate limiter per tenant (Free: 100/min, Pro: 10K/min)
   - Protobuf decode + schema version check
   - Publish to NATS JetStream stream `events.{tenant_id}`
   - `GET /healthz` — K8s readiness probe
   - `GET /metrics` — Prometheus metrics endpoint
   - Graceful shutdown: drain connections + flush NATS
5. Write Go integration tests: API → NATS → verify message

### Week 3: ClickHouse + Analytics Writer

6. Create ClickHouse schema (`cloud/internal/clickhouse/schema.sql`):
   - `events` table (ReplicatedMergeTree, partitioned by month)
   - ORDER BY (tenant_id, project_id, toDate(timestamp), tool_name, event_id)
   - 5 materialized views: cost_by_project_daily, savings_by_layer_hourly, productivity_by_dev_weekly, waste_by_pattern_daily, security_alerts
   - Row policy for tenant isolation
   - TTL: 90 days (Free/Pro), 365 days (Enterprise)
7. Implement analytics writer (`cloud/cmd/writer/main.go`):
   - NATS JetStream consumer (durable consumer group)
   - Batch insert to ClickHouse (10K rows/batch, flush every 5s)
   - Backpressure: if CH insert fails, NATS Nak + retry
   - Prometheus metrics: insert rate, latency, error count
8. Set up docker-compose for local dev:
   - NATS (with JetStream enabled)
   - ClickHouse (single-node dev mode)
   - Ingest API
   - Analytics Writer
9. Write integration tests: event → API → NATS → Writer → ClickHouse → query

### Week 4-5: Dashboard

10. Initialize Next.js app (`dashboard/`):
    - App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui
    - WorkOS AuthKit for auth (`@workos-inc/authkit-nextjs`)
    - TanStack Query for server state
    - Recharts for charts
11. Implement Go Query API (add to `cloud/cmd/ingest/` or separate service):
    - `GET /v1/overview?tenant_id=X` — org summary (total cost, savings, devs)
    - `GET /v1/projects/:id/stats` — per-project cost + savings
    - `GET /v1/developers/:id/stats` — per-dev efficiency
    - `GET /v1/productivity?tenant_id=X` — PR velocity, cycle time, acceptance rate
    - All queries hit materialized views (not raw events table)
    - JWT auth from WorkOS, extract tenant_id from token
12. Build dashboard pages:
    - `/overview` — org-level cards: total tokens saved, cost saved ($), compression ratio, active devs. Line chart: savings over time. Bar chart: savings by layer
    - `/projects/:id` — per-project: daily cost trend, top commands by waste, dev breakdown
    - `/developers/:id` — per-dev: session efficiency, tokens/PR, command frequency
    - `/productivity` — team: PRs merged/week, cycle time trend, build success rate
    - `/settings` — team invite, role management (admin/manager/dev/viewer), billing link
13. Implement RBAC in dashboard:
    - Admin: all pages + settings
    - Manager: all pages, team settings (no billing)
    - Developer: own metrics + team aggregates
    - Viewer: read-only all pages (for CFO/board access)

### Week 6: Polish + Deploy

14. Deploy infrastructure:
    - ClickHouse Cloud (or self-hosted on Hetzner/GCP for cost)
    - NATS on K8s (3-node JetStream cluster)
    - Go services on K8s (2 replicas each, HPA)
    - Dashboard on Vercel
15. Set up monitoring:
    - Prometheus + Grafana for Go services + ClickHouse
    - Vercel Analytics for dashboard
    - PagerDuty alerts: ingest error rate >1%, CH replication lag >60s
16. Load testing (k6):
    - Target: 50K events/sec sustained for 10 minutes
    - Verify ClickHouse query performance under load (<500ms p99)
17. End-to-end test: CLI install → login → coding session → events appear in dashboard
18. Stripe integration for Pro tier billing ($12/dev/month)
19. Landing page + docs site for launch

